Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: allow cgroup namespace root to host controllers

DroidSpaces uses a container-specific cgroup as the root of a new cgroup
namespace. Its monitor process is intentionally kept in that cgroup so the
namespace root maps to the container cgroup. On cgroup v2 this conflicts with
the normal no-internal-process restriction when nested workloads (Docker,
systemd) need controllers below the namespace root.

Treat the current cgroup namespace root as mixable, like the real cgroup root.
This is limited to the namespace root visible to the current task and leaves
ordinary cgroup hierarchy semantics unchanged.

--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
@@ -330,7 +330,15 @@ static bool cgroup_is_mixable(struct cgroup *cgrp)
 	 * root and a parent of resource domains at the same time.
 	 */
-	return !cgroup_parent(cgrp);
+	if (!cgroup_parent(cgrp))
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * A container cgroup is commonly used as the cgroup namespace root.
+	 * DroidSpaces intentionally keeps its monitor in that cgroup so the
+	 * namespace root maps to the container. Treat that namespace root as
+	 * mixable so nested cgroup v2 controllers can be enabled there.
+	 */
+	return cgrp == current_cgns_cgroup_dfl();
 }
 
 /* can @cgrp become a thread root? should always be true for a thread root */
